Could be that your dxaccounts died once and left files locked.

Have you tried rebooting? That's the first one to do.

If that doesnt help, well... It means that it's not OS lock on those
files, but a lock file itself. Try tracing dxaccounts. It could be
painful. See strace command. If that doesn't help you could use auditing
tool as a tracer. Turn on auditing for the machine and audit all file
access system calls for root. You'll see where it fails.

I hope this helped you. Personally, I never ran into something like
that. On the other hand, I've never had any trouble with dxaccounts. I
use enhanced security, do you use it?

Nix.



