Dara Ghahremani wrote:
> 
> I would like to change the "datasize" parameter that is listed when the
> "limit" command is used. Unfortunately, I can find no man page for this or

just type :

# sysconfig -q proc

you'll find per-proc-datasize (the default) and max-per-proc-datasize
(spell check, i've no syetm right now)

to add this, add these lines to /etc/sysconfigtab :

proc:
per-proc-datasize = new value

If you need more than 1 Go, you must also change the value of maxvas in
vm subsystem :
maxvas is maximum virtual address size of a process, system wide.

# sysconfig - q vm

you'll find maxvas

add these lines to /etc/sysconfigtab

vm:
maxvas = new value

After that, reboot, and check with sysconfig, and csh limit that life
can go on.

cheers
