C-shell (csh) command 'limit' shows datasize, and csh command 'unlimit' 
raises it from the default 'soft limit' value to a 'hard' limit.

Use commend '/sbin/sysconfig -q proc' to look at the values of parameters 
per-proc-data-size and max-per-proc-data-size. They're documented in the 
System Tuning and Performance Management online document under Process 
Subsystem Attributes.
 


